>> title: Sweet Tart Shell
>> category: Pastry & Doughs
>> tags: pastry, tart, butter, dough, oven
>> counters: Bakery, Dim Sum Counter, Panadería
>> aka: pâte sucrée, pate sucree, sweet shortcrust, tart crust, blind-baked shell
>> pairs-with: pastry-cream, lemon-curd
>> servings: 8
>> time: 2 hr 25 min
>> slack: narrow — a warm dough shrinks down the sides of the pan as it bakes, and there is no pressing it back up

>> step: cream the butter and sugar
Cream @unsalted butter{1/2%cup}(113 g; softened) with @powdered sugar{1/2%cup}(60 g) and @fine sea salt{1/4%tsp}(1.5 g).

>> step: beat in the yolk
Beat @egg yolk{1%large}(18 g) and @vanilla extract{1%tsp}(5 mL) into @&(~1)creamed butter{}.

>> step: work in the flours, just to clumps
Work @all-purpose flour{1 1/4%cup}(160 g) and @almond flour{1/4%cup}(25 g) into @&(~1)yolk mixture{} just until it clumps.

>> step: press into a disc, chill 1 hour
Press @&(~1)dough{} into a disc, wrap, and ~chill{60%min}.

>> step: roll out, line the pan, chill 30 min
Roll @&(~1)chilled dough{} out on a board dusted with @flour for the board{2%Tbs}(16 g), line a #9-in tart pan{}, and ~chill{30%min}.

>> step: blind bake 350°F (175°C) 20 min, weights out, 12 min more
Line @&(~1)tart shell{} with parchment and @dried beans{2%cup}(pie weights), ~bake{20%min} in a 350°F (175°C) #oven{}, then lift the beans out and ~bake{12%min} more.
